            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-700 mb-2">The Honest Expectation</p>
            <p class="text-amber-900 text-sm leading-relaxed">Expect a well-applied 1-part epoxy paint to last <strong>2–5 years</strong> in light-to-moderate traffic before it needs a recoat, versus <strong>5–20+ years</strong> for a properly installed 2-part epoxy system. If that trade-off works for your space and your budget, keep reading. If you're coating a daily-driver garage floor, read our <a href="/best-epoxy-garage-floor-kit" class="text-amber-900 underline font-bold">epoxy garage floor kit guide</a> instead.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

